(7260203, 1128711, 108580, '<td valign="top">Ja nee. You''ve done it again :) I''m impressed by the B&amp;W conversion which is very well handled btw. Top 10 and a good chance of Top 3. Perhaps the lack of a raised arm hiker might hurt the score a bit here (DPC) or rather had you included a hiker it may have gotten a few more higher scores. Personally I prefer it pristine and without anything human.</td>', 'Ja nee. You''ve done it again :) I''m impressed by the B&W conversion which is very well handled btw. Top 10 and a good chance of Top 3. Perhaps the lack of a raised arm hiker might hurt the score a bit here (DPC) or rather had you included a hiker it may have gotten a few more higher scores. Personally I prefer it pristine and without anything human.', '2014-09-07 06:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7260211, 1127605, 114233, '<td valign="top">Cracker of an image. Landscapes are just landscapes and then there are special landscapes - this is one of those. The human element adds to this shot. Remove the human and it is just a landscape with some nice sun rays in the BG. but with the human element it shows the scale and reminds us somewhat of the dangers of the big mountains. Respect the mountains and you end up with great shots like this. <br/> <br/>I remember this pinnacle on my first hike in this area. You march for hours to get to this spot and after a short climb you come over this little saddle (with the pinnacle on your right) and look up at the Mnweni pass looking where you still have to go. <br/>It took my breath away then and it did on this occasion too. Looking back up from where we just came down on this hike: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1129230" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/110000-114999/114233/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1129230.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/110000-114999/114233/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1129230.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/110000-114999/114233/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1129230.jpg"/></a>. It was a bit daunting standing on top of the pinnacle with a blustery wind blowing and a huge drop to the right but in the end I''m glad Rian forced me to do it (well asked kindly in a stern voice :-) ). Glad my weary legs held me upright. <br/> <br/>Lovely conversion but sadly these small dimensions don''t do it justice!</td>', 'Cracker of an image. Landscapes are just landscapes and then there are special landscapes - this is one of those. The human element adds to this shot. Remove the human and it is just a landscape with some nice sun rays in the BG. but with the human element it shows the scale and reminds us somewhat of the dangers of the big mountains. Respect the mountains and you end up with great shots like this.  I remember this pinnacle on my first hike in this area. You march for hours to get to this spot and after a short climb you come over this little saddle (with the pinnacle on your right) and look up at the Mnweni pass looking where you still have to go. It took my breath away then and it did on this occasion too. Looking back up from where we just came down on this hike: . It was a bit daunting standing on top of the pinnacle with a blustery wind blowing and a huge drop to the right but in the end I''m glad Rian forced me to do it (well asked kindly in a stern voice :-) ). Glad my weary legs held me upright.  Lovely conversion but sadly these small dimensions don''t do it justice!', '2014-09-07 09:49:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7260212, 1128826, 115814, '<td valign="top">Terrific sky and nice environmental framing... just a bit too much frame and not enough subject for me. It might be strengthened by cropping out the sky on the right.</td>', 'Terrific sky and nice environmental framing... just a bit too much frame and not enough subject for me. It might be strengthened by cropping out the sky on the right.', '2014-09-07 09:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(7260213, 1128189, 114233, '<td valign="top">Great image and should do really well. <br/>Something just seems to be wrong with the rock / sky on the left - like bad chromatic aberration and the rocks are soft like they weren''t sharpened enough. Perhaps your focal distance was too far away (like on the lighthouse) and didn''t use the hyperfocal distance?<br/>Still a great shot though.</td>', 'Great image and should do really well. Something just seems to be wrong with the rock / sky on the left - like bad chromatic aberration and the rocks are soft like they weren''t sharpened enough. Perhaps your focal distance was too far away (like on the lighthouse) and didn''t use the hyperfocal distance?Still a great shot though.', '2014-09-07 09:56:43.000000', NULL, 1),
